id: pm-rust-rfuc
title: "Lock contention on Windows presents as access denied, and the native binary treated it as a fatal filesystem error"
description: "On Windows a deleted file stays in a pending-delete state until every handle to it closes, and an open against a file in that state fails with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED rather than with already-exists or not-found. create_lock_file matched only ErrorKind::AlreadyExists, so a writer releasing its lock made a concurrent writer's create fail with PmRustError::Io and abort the mutation instead of retrying inside the configured wait budget. The read of the incumbent lock sat in the same window and had the same defect. Every Unix job passed; only the Windows runner reached the window, and only under real multi-process contention."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: "area:concurrency","platform:windows","severity:data-safety","type:defect"
created_at: "2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T06:21:42.602Z"
deadline: "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T06:21:42.577Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T06:21:42.577Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "A lock-path open or read that fails with AlreadyExists, PermissionDenied or NotFound is reported as a lock conflict and retried inside the wait budget; any other error keeps its own filesystem diagnostic; both arms are covered by tests that fail when the classification is narrowed back to AlreadyExists; coverage stays at 100 percent on every metric."
resolution: "lock_error_is_contention treats AlreadyExists, PermissionDenied and NotFound on a lock path as contention, so both the create and the incumbent read retry inside the caller's wait budget. Any other error keeps its own filesystem diagnostic."
expected_result: "A writer releasing its lock no longer aborts a concurrent writer's mutation on Windows; a lock that never frees still fails, and fails as a lock conflict."
actual_result: "Narrowing the classification back to AlreadyExists fails both new tests; restoring it passes. Gates: cargo fmt --check 0, clippy -D warnings 0, cargo test --all-targets --all-features 141 passed 0 failed, llvm-cov --branch 100.00 percent regions / functions / lines / branches."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-kgfh,related,"2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z",claude,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z",claude,"Found because the concurrency contract now asserts every rejection carries the lock-conflict diagnostic. The tolerant version added one round earlier would have counted these two dead writers as writers the budget did not admit,and passed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z",claude,"Observed on the runner: 'pm-rust: filesystem operation failed at ...locks/sample-load.lock: Access is denied. (os error 5)',twice in one run of 24 writers."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z",claude,A platform's presentation of an ordinary condition is not the condition changing. Windows reports a busy or releasing file as access denied; matching only the Unix presentation turns routine contention into an aborted write.
