  cargo test --lib windows_pending_delete_reads_as_lock_contention_not_as_a_fault,project,300,claude,"2026-08-28T06:21:26.582Z",local_mutation,feat/rust-native-mutations-and-conformance
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  tests/concurrency_contract.rs,project,the assertion that surfaced it
close_reason: fixed
body: "This defect was invisible until the concurrency contract was made to keep each rejected writer's diagnostic. The previous round had relaxed that test to tolerate a short admission count, which is right in itself, but it collapsed every rejection to a boolean. Under that assertion this run would have reported success: the writers that died on ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED would simply have counted as writers the budget did not admit. The failing assertion that found it is the one added in pm-rust-kgfh."
